Dragon Burst 0196: the UI thread no longer spins in SDL_WaitEvent on Android

On Android SDL_WaitEvent pumps the events with a poll sentinel each pass, and adding the sentinel wakes the Android
event wait (Android_SendLifecycleEvent WAKE), so the wait never blocked: the UI thread (SDLThread) used a whole core
with the Renut, SDL_UpdateJoysticks and clock_gettime on a loop (simpleperf, RG Cube and Odin 3, 2026-10-29). The
loop turns the sentinel off with SDL_HINT_POLL_SENTINEL (public SDL API; SDL itself is not changed). Nothing here
uses SDL_PollEvent's end-of-cycle stop.

diff --git a/src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp b/src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp
--- a/src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp
@@ -87,6 +87,13 @@
 
 int SDLWindowedAppContext::RunMainMessageLoop() {
   StartUIWatchdog();
+#if REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID
+  // Dragon Burst: no SDL poll sentinel. On Android SDL_WaitEvent pumps the events with a sentinel each pass, and
+  // adding the sentinel wakes the Android event wait, so the wait never blocked: the UI thread used a whole core
+  // (SDL_UpdateJoysticks and the clock on a loop, simpleperf on the RG Cube, 2026-10-29). Nothing here uses
+  // SDL_PollEvent's end-of-cycle stop.
+  SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_POLL_SENTINEL, "0");
+#endif
   while (!HasQuitFromUIThread()) {
     SDL_Event event;
